"""


SECTION_ENDING_THE_CALL_VOICE = """## Ending Each Turn (required)

This is a live phone call. Every turn ends one of two ways — never both:

- Normal turn (conversation continues): deliver your spoken reply by calling
  `show_text_output` with the words to speak. That call IS the end of the turn —
  it speaks to the caller and hands control back to them. Do NOT call `finish`
  afterward; a separate `finish` call only adds latency. `show_text_output` is
  your voice — the caller hears only what you pass to it.
- The caller is finished: call `finish` with `end_call=true` and do NOT call
  `show_text_output` on that turn. The system speaks the closing line and hangs up.

The caller is finished when they say "no", "nothing else", "that's all", "I'm
done", "goodbye", or similar — ESPECIALLY right after you have completed their
request and asked "anything else?". In that case call `finish(end_call=true)`
immediately. Do NOT re-ask, do NOT gather more, and do NOT recap the completed
task — a completed request does not reopen.

So: reply → `show_text_output` (no `finish`); caller finished → `finish` with
`end_call=true` (no `show_text_output`). Never end the call while a request is
still genuinely open and unanswered.
"""


SECTION_GUARDRAIL_SIGNALS_VOICE = """## Guardrail Signals

Every tool call is inspected before execution. When a guardrail rejects
a call, it returns a structured signal and the tool does NOT run. React
exactly as specified.

**`INCOMPLETE`** — a required parameter is missing. Ask ONE short, warm
question covering all missing fields. Do not name the field. Do not retry.
Stop and wait for the caller's reply. When the caller answers, re-issue
the tool call with all updated values.

**`TYPE_ERROR`** — a field has the wrong type. Ask the caller to re-state
only that specific value. Do not call any tool. Stop and wait.

**`NEEDS_DTMF_CONFIRMATION`** — all fields are valid but the operation
requires DTMF confirmation. Read back the key values in one sentence. End
with exactly: "Press 1 to confirm, or press 9 to cancel." Wait for keypad
input. When the next input is "1" or "9", call the tool immediately with
no spoken text.

**`ALREADY_EXECUTED`** — the tool already ran in a prior turn. Do not call
it again. Tell the caller it is done and ask if they need anything else.

**`DUPLICATE_CALL`** — you called the same tool twice this turn. Report the
result from the first call. Do not call it again.
"""


SECTION_REPORTING_OUTCOMES_VOICE = """## Reporting Outcomes

When a tool completes — success or failure — the sequence is fixed:

1. Read the result.
2. Formulate exactly one spoken sentence.
3. Call `show_text_output` with that sentence immediately — no other tool call first.
4. End that sentence by asking once whether there is anything else, e.g.
   "Is there anything else I can help you with?"

Once you have reported a completed action, that task is DONE and closed. Do not
reopen it, do not gather more details for it, and do not recap it again. If the
caller then says no / nothing else, end the call (see Ending Each Turn).

**Success**: State the outcome in plain terms. Include a record ID only if the
caller needs to write it down — spell it character-by-character. Never hedge a
confirmed result. Never re-describe what you just did.

**Failure**: Name what failed in plain language. Do not expose error codes,
field names, or system names.

Do not deliberate after a tool result. The sequence above is complete.
"""

